<svelte:head><title>Nolune — Design system</title></svelte:head>
{#if showBirth}<MoonBirth oncomplete={() => showBirth = false} />{/if}
<main class="system" inert={showBirth}>
 <header><a class="brand" href="/"><img src="/skins/moon/character.svg" alt="" width="32" height="32" />nolune</a><a href="/">Back to your companions ↗</a></header>
 <section class="intro"><div><p class="nl-eyebrow">Little Moon · Design system / 01</p><h1>A familiar language.<br />Room to grow.</h1><p>The shared visual foundation for Nolune’s client and landing. Calm surfaces, clear actions, and a little personality.</p></div><img src="/skins/moon/character.svg" width="180" height="180" alt="Little Moon" /></section>
 <nav aria-label="Design system sections"><a href="#palette">Palette</a><a href="#type">Typography</a><a href="#components">Components</a><a href="#conversation">Conversation</a><a href="#settings">Settings</a><a href="#companion">Companion state</a><a href="#spaces">Connected spaces</a><a href="#handoff">Handoff</a><a href="#principles">Principles</a></nav>
 <section id="palette"><p class="nl-eyebrow">01 / Color</p><h2>Plum, lavender, and breathing room.</h2><div class="swatches">{#each colors as [name, token, hex]}<article class="nl-panel swatch"><div style={`background:var(${token})`}></div><strong>{name}</strong><code>{token}</code><small>{hex}</small></article>{/each}</div></section>
 <section id="type"><p class="nl-eyebrow">02 / Typography</p><div class="two"><article class="nl-panel"><h2>Personality in the headlines.</h2><p>Fraunces · regular 400 · restrained tracking</p><p class="display-sample">A little more you.</p></article><article class="nl-panel"><h3>Clarity in the everyday.</h3><p>Bricolage Grotesque · body, buttons, navigation</p><p>Keep interface text direct and readable. Use sentence case and reserve the serif for welcoming moments.</p><code>JetBrains Mono — code and technical values</code></article></div></section>
 <section id="components"><p class="nl-eyebrow">03 / Components</p><h2>Useful, familiar, consistent.</h2><div class="two"><article class="nl-panel actions-panel"><h3>Actions</h3><div class="actions"><button class="nl-button nl-button-secondary" onclick={() => showBirth = true}>Replay moon arrival</button><button class="nl-button" onclick={() => saved = true}>Primary action</button><button class="nl-button nl-button-secondary" onclick={() => saved = false}>Reset example</button><button class="nl-button" disabled>Unavailable</button></div><p role="status">{saved ? 'Example action complete. No data was saved.' : 'Interactive examples only. No account changes.'}</p></article><article class="nl-panel"><label for="sample-name">Your name</label><input id="sample-name" class="nl-input" bind:value={sampleName} placeholder="What should Nolune call you?" /><p>{sampleName ? `Hello, ${sampleName}.` : 'Visible labels, comfortable spacing, and a clear focus ring.'}</p></article></div></section>
 <section id="conversation"><p class="nl-eyebrow">04 / Conversation</p><h2>Let the words do the work.</h2><p>Real Svelte AI Elements, styled for Little Moon. Try sending, stopping, attachments, and a failed send. This example runs locally without a backend.</p><ChatExample />
 <article class="nl-panel receipt-sample"><h3>Memory receipt</h3><p>Under an assistant reply, “Why did Nolune remember this?” lists the memories that shaped it: the canonical source, the excerpt that was recalled, how retrieval found it, a confidence bucket (never a score) and when. A source forgotten since the reply is said so. In the app each entry carries Inspect, Correct, Pin, Exclude from proactive use and Forget; a correction that conflicts with an earlier one shows both statements and asks which stays. Sample data; the controls need a running companion.</p><MemoryReceiptPanel slug="example" chatId="example" messageId="example-receipt" memories={sampleReceipt} readonly /></article></section>
 <section id="settings"><p class="nl-eyebrow">05 / Settings</p><h2>One panel, sectioned.</h2><p>Every settings page is one panel divided into rows: the section title and a one-line description on the left, its controls on the right. Sections are never separate cards, so uneven heights cannot leave gaps. The section nav is a segmented control. Example only; nothing here is saved.</p>
 <div class="settings-page ds-settings">
  <header class="settings-head"><h2 class="settings-title">Settings</h2><nav class="settings-nav" aria-label="Example settings sections">{#each [['companion', 'Companion'], ['connections', 'Connections'], ['advanced', 'Advanced']] as [id, label] (id)}<a href="#settings" class="settings-nav-link" class:settings-nav-active={exampleSection === id} aria-current={exampleSection === id ? 'page' : undefined} onclick={(e) => { e.preventDefault(); exampleSection = id; }}>{label}</a>{/each}</nav><p class="settings-lead">Presence, rhythm, initiative, and time.</p></header>
  <div class="settings-panel">
   <section class="settings-section"><div class="section-header"><div><h3 class="section-label">Companion</h3><p class="section-desc">Little Moon, your familiar presence across devices.</p></div>
</div><div class="section-body"><div class="setting-row"><span class="setting-label" id="ds-rhythm-label">Learn my rhythm</span><div class="setting-input-row"><button class="setting-btn" role="switch" aria-checked={exampleRhythm} aria-labelledby="ds-rhythm-label" onclick={() => (exampleRhythm = !exampleRhythm)}>{exampleRhythm ? 'On' : 'Off'}</button></div><p class="setting-hint">Keeps a bounded summary of when you tend to write, so check-ins land at good moments.</p></div>
</div></section>
   <section class="settings-section"><div class="section-header"><div><h3 class="section-label">Models</h3><p class="section-desc">A preset row says what its model cannot do as chips, and Test sends one short request without touching any chat.</p></div>
</div><div class="section-body"><ul class="preset-list" aria-label="Example preset"><li class="preset-row"><label class="preset-field">Name<input class="ext-input" type="text" value={examplePreset.name} readonly /></label><div class="preset-field"><span id="example-preset-provider">Provider</span><SettingSelect aria-labelledby="example-preset-provider" value="openrouter" options={[{ value: "openrouter", label: "OpenRouter" }]} disabled /></div><label class="preset-field preset-field-model">Model id<input class="ext-input" type="text" value={examplePreset.model} readonly /></label><button class="setting-btn setting-btn-danger preset-remove" type="button" disabled>Remove</button><div class="preset-foot">{#each exampleWarnings as warning (warning.id)}<span class="preset-chip" title={warning.detail}>{warning.chip}</span>{/each}<button class="nl-button-secondary preset-test" type="button" onclick={() => (exampleTested = !exampleTested)}>{exampleTested ? 'Reset' : 'Test'}</button>{#if exampleTested}<span class="preset-result preset-result-ok" role="status">{exampleTestCopy.text} (example)</span>{/if}</div></li></ul>{#each exampleWarnings as warning (warning.id)}<p class="setting-hint setting-warning">{warning.detail}</p>{/each}</div></section>
   <section class="settings-section"><div class="section-header"><div><h3 class="section-label">Codex</h3><p class="section-desc">A ChatGPT login through the local codex binary (#27): the tile names the release and its path, one state line, Log in or Log out, and while a login is pending the URL to open and the code to type. Sample statuses; the buttons need a running server.</p></div>
</div><div class="section-body"><div class="settings-nav ds-codex-nav" role="group" aria-label="Sample codex states">{#each [['pending', 'Pending login'], ['loggedIn', 'Logged in'], ['missing', 'Not installed']] as [id, label] (id)}<button type="button" class="settings-nav-link" class:settings-nav-active={codexSample === id} aria-pressed={codexSample === id} onclick={() => (codexSample = id)}>{label}</button>{/each}</div>{#key codexSample}<CodexLogin sample={codexSamples[codexSample]} />{/key}</div></section>
   <section class="settings-section"><div class="section-header"><div><h3 class="section-label">Companions</h3><p class="section-desc">Peer companions this one is paired with (#108): each row is its id, its state beside a color, who invited whom, where it is reached, and when something it signed last verified here. Sample records; Confirm and Revoke need a running companion.</p></div>
</div><div class="section-body"><ul class="ds-companions" aria-label="Sample companions">{#each sampleCompanions as peer (peer.id)}<CompanionRow {peer}>{#if peer.state === 'paired'}<PeerCapabilities peerShortId={peer.shortId} rows={sampleRows} open={true} />{/if}</CompanionRow>{/each}</ul></div></section>
   <section class="settings-section"><div class="section-header"><div><h3 class="section-label">Companion approvals</h3><p class="section-desc">Requests that asked the owner (#109): a pending row on the selected surface with one bounded scope and Allow or Deny; a decided row with Withdraw. Under each paired companion, what it may do folds out as one rule per intent and class with a shared Select (Default, Allowed, Asks you, Denied). Sample records; deciding needs a running companion.</p></div>
</div><div class="section-body"><div class="ds-companions"><PendingApprovals pending={samplePending} decided={sampleDecided} onapprove={async () => {}} ondeny={async () => {}} onwithdraw={async () => {}} /></div></div></section>
   <section class="settings-section"><div class="section-header"><div><h3 class="section-label">Companion inbox</h3><p class="section-desc">What paired companions delivered (#110): a request that needs the owner sits on the selected surface beside its approval, a settled one says what happened, and the quoted labels are the companion's own words. A delivered message itself appears in the conversation above, framed as untrusted. Sample records.</p></div>
</div><div class="section-body"><div class="ds-companions"><InboundIntents rows={sampleInbox} /></div></div></section>
   <section class="settings-section"><div class="section-header"><div><h3 class="section-label">Sent to companions</h3><p class="section-desc">What this companion asked paired companions for (#110), as the Activity page lists it: the request kind and the companion, this owner's own words as sent, one status word, and a line on how often it was tried and what came back. A request still on its way carries the lavender border, one that is over the destructive one. Sample records at a fixed clock.</p></div>
</div><div class="section-body"><div class="ds-companions"><PeerRequestList entries={sampleOutbox} now={1_800_000_000} /></div></div></section>
   <section class="settings-section"><div class="section-header"><div><h3 class="section-label">From companions</h3><p class="section-desc">What paired companions proposed (#111), as the Activity page lists it above the commitments: a meeting, a reminder, or a task handed over, each a card like a handoff card with the companion's words in the dashed untrusted panel the conversation uses, one status phrase, a line saying nothing is written until you accept, and Accept and Dismiss. A card that waits for you carries the lavender border, a decided one the plain border, a lapsed one the destructive border. Sample records at a fixed clock; deciding here is simulated and writes nothing.</p></div>
</div><div class="section-body"><div class="ds-companions"><ul class="ds-proposals">{#each sampleProposals as proposal (proposal.id)}<li><PeerProposalCard {proposal} now={1_800_000_000} onaccept={() => exampleAcceptProposal(proposal)} ondismiss={() => exampleDismissProposal(proposal)} onupdated={proposalUpdated} /></li>{/each}</ul></div></div></section>
   <section class="settings-section"><div class="section-header"><div><h3 class="section-label">Server <span class="owner-badge">This server</span></h3><p class="section-desc">Owner badges mark controls that apply to the whole server.</p></div>
</div><div class="section-body"><div class="setting-row"><label class="setting-label" for="ds-port">Port</label><div class="setting-input-row"><input class="setting-input" id="ds-port" type="number" value="26559" readonly /><button class="setting-btn" type="button" disabled>Save</button></div><p class="setting-hint">Inputs keep 16px text and a visible focus ring. Actions stay 44px tall.</p></div>
</div></section>
  </div>
 </div></section>
 <section id="companion"><p class="nl-eyebrow">06 / Companion state</p><h2>The moon says what is really happening.</h2><p>Every state is derived from a runtime event and resolved in this priority order. Each moon shows the face and motion the state maps to (<code>lib/companion/expressions.js</code>); the sentence beside it is the accessible status text, a live region whose focus links to the related computer, conversation, Activity run or handoff card, so the state reads without motion. Examples are reduced live by <code>lib/companion/state.js</code>; the links lead to the companion’s own routes.</p><label class="state-toggle"><input type="checkbox" bind:checked={stillMoons} /> Reduced motion: hold every moon still, keep the words</label><ol class="states">{#each companionStates as s, i (s.kind)}<li class="nl-panel state" data-kind={s.kind}><MoonExpression kind={s.kind} size={72} reducedMotion={stillMoons} /><div><strong><code class="state-rank">{i + 1}</code>{s.label}</strong><CompanionStatus class="state-text" state={s.state} slug={DEFAULT_COMPANION_SLUG} /><small>{s.source}</small><small class="state-look">{s.look.asset.split('/').pop()} · {stillMoons || s.look.motion === 'none' ? 'still' : s.look.motion}</small></div></li>{/each}</ol></section>
 <section id="spaces"><p class="nl-eyebrow">07 / Connected spaces</p><h2>Every place it can act, one list.</h2><p>The Computers tab and Settings › Connections list the server home first, then desktops: online by name, then offline by last seen. Each row pairs its state word with a color, shows what the desktop reported (the Cua driver's grants, the actions its app executes, the driver), and carries one hint per thing to do. Rename is inline; Forget, on an offline row only, asks once before it drops the record. Rows are viewed by <code>lib/computers/spaces.js</code> from sample records at a fixed clock; renaming or forgetting here changes nothing on a server.</p><ul class="spaces">{#each sampleSpaces as space (space.id)}<SpaceRow {space} onrename={space.canRename ? sampleRename(space.id) : undefined} onforget={space.canForget ? sampleForget(space.id) : undefined} />{/each}</ul></section>
 <section id="handoff"><p class="nl-eyebrow">08 / Handoff</p><h2>Pick a task up where you are.</h2><p>A handoff card (#82) is derived from the task record and the known computers, so it reads the same while the computer it started on is offline. Continue here, Continue on…, Keep there, and Dismiss are the four decisions; a preview names the destination and every check before anything runs. Example only, with simulated computers: studio is offline, Travel Laptop is ready, old-mini is not responding.</p><div class="handoff-example"><HandoffCard card={exampleCard} machines={exampleMachines} hereId="mac-b" now={exampleNow} onpreview={examplePreview} onaccept={exampleAccept} onkeep={exampleKeep} ondismiss={exampleDismiss} onupdated={(card) => (exampleCard = card)} /><button class="nl-button nl-button-secondary" onclick={() => (exampleCard = exampleHandoff())}>Reset example</button></div><h3>Resume my work</h3><p>The opt-in ritual (#83) offers at most one task per trigger, from the task records alone: it says which task, why it was picked (priority, deadline, blockers, recency, a ready computer), and why now (you asked, you came back after a break, a computer the task names reconnected). Review and continue leads to the handoff card above; Not now, Snooze, and Never this task answer the ritual. Example only.</p><div class="handoff-example">{#if exampleOffer}<ResumeBanner offer={exampleOffer} now={exampleNow} reviewHref="#handoff" onrefuse={answerExample} onsnooze={answerExample} ondismiss={answerExample} />{:else}<p>Answered. Nothing was continued.</p>{/if}<button class="nl-button nl-button-secondary" onclick={() => (exampleOffer = exampleResume())}>Reset example</button></div></section>
 <section id="principles"><p class="nl-eyebrow">09 / Principles</p><div class="two"><article class="nl-panel"><h3>A companion, with restraint.</h3><p>Use the moon as a recognizable presence. Keep working surfaces quiet. Use the same plum panels and lavender actions across settings, content, and conversation views. Keep loading, empty, and error states distinct.</p></article><article class="nl-panel"><h3>Accessible by default.</h3><p>44px controls, visible keyboard focus, readable secondary text, and reduced-motion support. Dialogs contain keyboard focus and restore it when closed. Pair every status color with words.</p></article></div></section>
 <footer>Implementation reference: docs/design-system.md · Tokens: client/src/lib/styles/tokens.css</footer>
</main>
<style>
.handoff-example{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px;max-width:720px;align-items:flex-start}.handoff-example>:global(.handoff),.handoff-example>:global(.resume){width:100%}.system{height:100%;overflow:auto;padding:0 max(24px,calc((100vw - 1080px)/2)) 48px;background:var(--background);scroll-behavior:smooth;scroll-padding-top:24px}header{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;padding:24px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);gap:16px;font-size:13px;color:var(--text-secondary)}.brand{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;font:500 24px var(--font-body);color:var(--foreground)}.intro{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:40px;align-items:center}.intro>div{max-width:650px}h1{font:400 clamp(2.5rem,5vw,4.5rem)/1.1 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.035em;margin:20px 0}h2{font:400 32px/1.2 var(--font-display);margin:12px 0 24px}h3{font:500 18px var(--font-body);margin:0 0 20px}p{font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--text-secondary)}nav{display:flex;gap:24px;flex-wrap:wrap;padding-bottom:24px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);font-size:14px;color:var(--primary)}section{padding:40px 0}.swatches{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:16px}.swatch{padding:12px;display:grid;gap:6px}.swatch>div{height:80px;border-radius:8px;border:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px}code,small{color:var(--text-muted);font-size:12px}code{font-family:var(--font-mono)}.two{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}.display-sample{font:400 36px var(--font-display);color:var(--foreground)}.actions-panel{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:20px}.actions-panel h3,.actions-panel p{margin:0}.actions{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:12px}label{display:block;font-size:14px;margin-bottom:12px}.ds-settings{height:auto;padding:0;overflow:visible}.states{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px}.spaces,.ds-companions,.ds-proposals{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;max-width:720px}.ds-proposals{gap:12px}.state{display:flex;gap:16px;padding:16px;align-items:flex-start}.state>:global(.moon-expression){flex-shrink:0}.state strong{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;font-size:14px;color:var(--foreground)}.state-rank{font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);min-width:1.5em}.state :global(.state-text){margin:4px 0 8px;font-size:14px;color:var(--foreground)}.state small{display:block;line-height:1.5}.state-look{margin-top:4px;font-family:var(--font-mono)}.state-toggle{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;min-height:44px;margin:0 0 16px;font-size:14px;color:var(--text-secondary)}.state-toggle input{width:18px;height:18px;accent-color:var(--primary)}footer{padding-top:24px;border-top:1px solid var(--border);font-size:12px;color:var(--text-muted);line-height:1.7}@media(max-width:650px){.two{grid-template-columns:1fr}.states{grid-template-columns:1fr}.swatches{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}.intro{gap:16px}.intro>img{width:80px;height:80px}h1{font-size:2.4rem}header>a:last-child{font-size:11px}nav{gap:16px}.system{padding-left:20px;padding-right:20px}section{padding:28px 0}}
.ds-codex-nav{margin-bottom:12px}.ds-codex-nav button{background:none;border:0;cursor:pointer}.ds-codex-nav button.settings-nav-active{background:var(--primary)}.receipt-sample{max-width:800px;margin-top:20px}.receipt-sample h3{margin:0 0 8px;font:500 18px/1.3 var(--font-body)}.receipt-sample p{margin:0 0 12px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--text-secondary)}
</style>
